# Auto-deploy Open Play (testing + hosted site)

## Scope

Applies whenever **`Programs/Pickleball/live/`** (deployed HTML/JS) or **`Programs/Pickleball/testing/`** (unit tests, `local-test.js`, mirrors) is edited.

## Agent must run (from `Website/` = repo root)

1. **`npm run local-test:sync`** — refresh `local-page/` mirrors so local QA matches `live/`.
2. **`npm test`** — must pass before deploy.
3. **`npm run deploy:openplay`** — push **`Programs/Pickleball/live`** to **Firebase Hosting** (`firebase.json` → `hosting.public`). This updates the **hosted testing/staging URL** (e.g. `*.web.app` / custom domain for project `pickleball-advanced-open-play`).

If deploy fails (auth): run **`firebase login`** once locally, or configure CI secret **`FIREBASE_TOKEN`** from **`firebase login:ci`**.

## CI (no manual step after push)

On push to **`main`** / **`master`**, **`.github/workflows/deploy-openplay-firebase-hosting.yml`** runs **`firebase deploy --only hosting`** when the paths above change. Requires **`FIREBASE_TOKEN`** in GitHub repo **Settings → Secrets**.

## Not auto here

- **Database rules** — use **`npm run firebase:deploy-rules`** when **`database.rules.json`** changes (or **`npm run deploy:openplay:all`** for hosting + rules together).

## Do not deploy

Gitignored mirrors (`local-page/`, `testing/local-page/`) — generated only; **Hosting serves `live/`** per `firebase.json`.
